**`txtar/archive.go`** — new method:

```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false if no such file exists.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	if a == nil {
		return nil, false
	}
	for i := range a.Files {
		if a.Files[i].Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — new test `TestLookup` covering:
- **Found case**: `Lookup("foo.txt")` returns a non-nil `*File` with correct `Name` and `Data`, and `ok == true`.
- **Not-found case**: `Lookup("nope.txt")` returns `nil, false`.

All tests pass (`ok golang.org/x/tools/txtar`).

